  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale  \nWe propose a hybrid particle swarm optimization (PSO) with mutation to minimize C\u2085. PSO is well-suited for non-convex problems due to its global search capability, while mutations introduce controlled random perturbations to escape local optima. This approach combines exploration (particle movement) with exploitation (mutation) to balance search effectiveness. The algorithm uses the initial_h_values as a starting point to leverage existing progress and maintains feasibility through repair steps.\n\n2. Mathematical specification  \nVariables: h \u2208 \u211d^n_points, h[i] \u2208 [0,1], \u03a3h = n_points / 2  \nObjective: minimize C\u2085 = max\u2096 \u222bh(x)(1 - h(x+k)) dx, equivalent to max convolution over shifts  \nConstraints: 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1, \u03a3h[i] = n_points / 2  \nPSO dynamics: v = w*v + c1*rand*(pbest - current) + c2*rand*(gbest - current) + mutation noise  \n\n3. Implementation procedure  \na. Initialization:  \n- Extract initial_h_values if available, else create a triangular pulse  \n- Initialize 100 particles around initial_h_values with small random perturbations  \n- Ensure each particle satisfies constraints via repair\n\nb. PSO loop:  \n- Evaluate C\u2085 for all particles  \n- Update personal best and global best  \n- Update velocities using PSO formula with inertia, cognitive, social terms  \n- Add Gaussian noise to velocities for exploration  \n- Update positions, apply repair to enforce constraints  \n\nc. Mutation:  \n- Every 25 iterations, mutate 10% of particles by randomly perturbing 20% of their values  \n- Clip and repair mutated particles  \n\nd. Termination:  \n- Stop when budget exhausted or no improvement for 100 iterations  \n\n4. Search choices and useful variations  \n- Inertia weight w: starts at 0.9, decreases to 0.4  \n- Cognitive (c1=2), social (c2=2) coefficients  \n- Mutation rate: 10% with sigma=0.1  \n- Population size: 100 particles  \n\n5. Compute budget and robustness  \n- Per iteration cost: O(n\u00b2) evaluations + O(n) repairs  \n- Total iterations: up to 400 within 600s  \n- Mutation operations maintain diversity and prevent stagnation  \n\n6. Validation and return contract  \n- Ensure all h[i] \u2208 [0,1] and \u03a3h = n_points / 2  \n- Recompute C\u2085 with the evaluator for best solution  \n- Return best particle, its C\u2085, and n_points",
